A: Your code seems to have mixed up the elements of a PexTestCase. Could you please also provide the method for which you are trying to establish a Contract? Please note that this question might be closed as it doesn't clearly specify what Pex Contract tests are attempted to be conducted.

A: Unfortunately, it looks like some of the information you've provided is incorrect or omitted. The code that you've provided doesn't look a lot like a Pex Contract test method. Here's an example of how you might set up a Pex Contract test for the ArrayList Get() method:

public void PUT_GetContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, [PexIgnoreDelegate] Predicate<int> ignore, [PexPositive]int index)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index < arrList.Count && index >= 0);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    object Old_index = arrList.Get(index);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Get(index);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

    bool New_containsNewRet = arrList.Contains(New_Ret);

    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_index", Old_index);    
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_ret", New_Ret);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);
    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_containsNewRet", New_containsNewRet);

    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ the array contains New_Ret 
    //  and the array count is not changed
    Debug.Assert(New_containsNewRet == true && Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);
}

This example expects a previously initialized ArrayList, a Predicate delegate that's ignored during testing, and an index within the ArrayList's range. It will then assert that the ArrayList's contents and count remain unchanged when retrieving a value from an existing index.

Please review the code carefully to ensure all parameters and assumptions are correctly implemented. If the code still doesn't provide the expected contract for the ArrayList.Get() function, please provide more precise information about the issue you're experiencing.

